    "title": "Safer Safe Workspace gating and a hardened desktop harness",
    "intro": "Today's nightly tightens where Safe Workspace can be offered and gives the desktop harness a more resilient path to finding, staging, and syncing its sidecar binary and skills. The result is fewer confusing prompts in non-Git projects and a steadier bootstrap on packaged Mac, Windows, and Linux builds.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "4:54 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-29T11:54:16.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-29T11:54:16.000Z",
        "title": "Safe Workspace hidden outside Git-backed projects",
        "summary": "The agent chat panel now checks eligibility before offering Safe Workspace, so folders that aren't Git repositories no longer see an option that would immediately fail.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added a read-only preflight that only advertises Safe Workspace when the linked desktop folder resolves to a Git repository with at least one commit, avoiding any attempt to initialise or mutate a user's source folder.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "399c6144989f41660a252f27b3d992fa6da4f25e"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Exposed a new eligibility endpoint and wired the Agent Chat Panel to hide the Safe Workspace affordance when the backend reports it unavailable.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "399c6144989f41660a252f27b3d992fa6da4f25e"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Turned previously opaque Git failures during workspace prep into clearer 'not a Git repository' and 'repository must have at least one commit' unsupported errors.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "399c6144989f41660a252f27b3d992fa6da4f25e"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
